            <ArticleTitle>Management of acute postoperative pain after oral surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-111, viii</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cden.2011.09.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article provides a brief review of the acute pain mechanism as it relates to the effects of a surgical insult. A brief understanding of the physiologic modulation of acute pain establishes a rational framework for the concept of preemptive and postoperative analgesia. A brief review of commonly used analgesic agents is presented. Research in pain management and new drug development is ongoing as new concepts in neurophysiology and pharmacology are being elucidated.</AbstractText>
